+## 173 - (Fixed/Improved) Base AdvCiv issue: Live first-settler scoring reused hidden map-generation surroundings
+
+Screenshots/files for this issue: [google drive folder link](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/18GJifCcCBZbrKR5nT84FmXgdHZJxtaMz?usp=sharing).
+
+In the Berlin test, the starting settler initially founded at fresh-water `(36,9)`, whose BFC contained ten Tundra tiles, instead of the greener `(33,13)` candidate with Rice, Cattle, Silver, four Grass Hills, and four peaks.
+
+The investigation found three related problems in live first-settler scoring:
+
+- Starting-capital evaluation also enabled the all-seeing mode intended for map generation, so fogged BFC terrain affected live movement decisions. Live first-settler evaluation now keeps the capital-specific weights while disabling all-seeing; fogged plots are neutral.
+- Once the tolerated very-bad-plot count was exceeded, every bad BFC slot was penalized instead of only the excess. The first-city allowance is now four, and only slots beyond it are penalized, so four peaks do not erase the value of the site's strong workable land.
+- After those fixes, Berlin moved to `(35,11)`. Compact found-value breakdown logging showed that `(33,13)` actually led `(35,11)` by `4569` to `3934` before final modifiers, but `adjustToStartingSurroundings` applied `-1482` to `(33,13)` versus `-480` to `(35,11)`, reversing them to `3087` and `3454`.
+
+| Site | Before modifiers | Starting-surroundings adjustment | Final |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| `(33,13)` | **4569** | **-1482** | 3087 |
+| `(35,11)` | 3934 | -480 | **3454** |
+| `(36,9)` | 3047 | -473 | 2574 |
+
+`adjustToStartingSurroundings` evaluates terrain out to range 6 and distances from every civilization's assigned starting plot. That is appropriate during all-seeing map generation/normalization, where it helps spread the assigned starts. Once play begins, however, the live first settler should choose its best revealed site even if that moves nearer to or farther from a neighbor; assigned-start spacing should not override candidate quality. Live first-settler scoring therefore skips this modifier by default, while map generation and normalization are unchanged. `SAS_AI_FOUND_FIRST_CITY_RUNTIME_STARTING_SURROUNDINGS_ADJUSTMENT_ENABLE=1` restores the old runtime adjustment.
+
+The new `FOUND_VALUE_BREAKDOWN` line records the exact additive components and each later modifier for level-3 first-city diagnostics; `selectionValue` and `recomputedValue` also verify that the logged breakdown matches the value used by the decision.
+
+Removing the runtime starting-surroundings adjustment eliminated the major artificial nerf to `(33,13)`, but did not by itself make Berlin settle there.
+
+Continued BBAI testing exposed additional overlapping first-city filters and scouting behavior that could still exclude or fail to reveal the best complete found-value candidate.
+
+- Recovery candidates now require a fully revealed BFC before interrupting bounded scouting, and when the scouting window ends the settler rechecks revealed reachable sites instead of blindly founding wherever scouting stopped. Candidate ranking uses complete first-city found value rather than separate food-bonus or food-environment filters; those diagnostics still decide whether a poor start warrants scouting.
+- Karakorum follow-up testing then exposed a broader bonus overvaluation: older SAS logic weighted bonus-improvement Food x3 and Production x2 before AdvCiv's obscure hardcoded nonlinear `evaluateSpecialYields` path weighted the aggregated yields again. Six resources contributed 5015 points to the low-food `(49,43)` candidate, overwhelming stronger river/grass alternatives. The redundant AdvCiv path is now disabled for reference, and actual bonus-improvement Food/Production/Commerce changes are valued once through simple XML tunables. Natural-yield weights were also externalized, while unsupported small Barbarian and first-era Commerce exceptions were disabled for one consistent valuation.
+- After these follow-up changes, Berlin naturally ranks fully revealed `(33,13)` above `(35,11)` by `4027` to `3957` and founds there in the save file 442 regression test. Save file 360 improved from tundra/resource-heavy `(49,43)` to river Grassland `(50,40)` with Pig and Maize; save file 431 selected reasonable river Grassland `(38,44)` in a generally poor starting region. Generic fog exploration can still delay founding or leave another promising BFC partly unrevealed, so targeted scouting remains a separate refinement.
+
+Fixed/improved with the help of GPT-5.5 (on Codex) thanks.

